'''wayboard''' (wā′bōrd), ''n.'' In ''mini'' tenacious clay formed by the deco the toadstone. Also written ''weigh-'' byshire, Eng.]

'''waybread''' (wā′bred), ''n.'' [Also ''wa'' ''weybrede, weibrede,'' < AS. ''wegbrǣ'' ''wegebrēde, wegebreide,'' LG. ''weegbr'' ''wegabreita,'' MHG. ''wegebreite,'' G. ''we'' ''vägbreda'' = Dan. ''vejbred''), plantai called as spreading along roads, road, + ''brǣdan,'' spread, < ''brād,'' ''bread''<sup>2</sup>.] The common plantain, ''Pl'' See cut under ''plantain.''

