'''waylayer''' (wā-lā′ėr or wā′lā″ėr), ''n.'' One who waylays; one who lies in wait for another.
{{smaller block|Wherever there are rich way-farers there also are sly and alert ''way-layers.''
{{right|''Landor'', Imag. Conv., Asinius Pollio and Licinius Calvus, i.}}}}

'''way-leave†''' (wā′lēv), ''n.'' Right of way.
{{smaller block|Another thing that is remarkable is their ''wayleaves''; for, when men have pieces of ground between the colliery}}

